{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836004",
      "title": "Dynamic & Conditional Styling with CSS Files & CSS Classes",
      "sourceHash": "8b51aefc0bba0c10c50bec58d1db53505603f2ff93c75708b490874d10c43ab6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.54,
          "end": 3.03,
          "en": "Pretty much all React applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.03,
          "end": 7.35,
          "en": "have parts in them that need to be styled dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.35,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "like we're doing it here with the inline styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 14.37,
          "en": "But as mentioned, inline styles have certain disadvantages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 17.1,
          "en": "which I don't wanna have here in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 20.4,
          "en": "and therefore, I'll switch back to using class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.4,
          "end": 23.133,
          "en": "and using my standalone CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 26.1,
          "en": "Though, of course, as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.1,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "you will learn about some other styling options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 30.663,
          "en": "later in this section as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 34.17,
          "en": "But as you can already see here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.17,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "you can, of course, also style elements conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 40.923,
          "en": "when you using extra CSS files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.06,
          "end": 46.86,
          "en": "typically achieved by adding a CSS class conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.86,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "Here, it's just important to note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 52.68,
          "en": "that you should then use ternary expression",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.68,
          "end": 55.5,
          "en": "and add undefined as a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.5,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "if you don't wanna have this conditional class applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "Because if you would use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "double ampersand shortcut here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 67.17,
          "en": "which technically would work, the result would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.17,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "if you reload the app that you get a warning here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 73.86,
          "en": "in the console because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.86,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "you now added false as a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 80.01,
          "en": "because with this trick here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.01,
          "end": 83.31,
          "en": "if this condition here is not met, if it's false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.31,
          "end": 87.84,
          "en": "you're now setting this here as a value for class name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.84,
          "end": 89.61,
          "en": "And since this is a Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.61,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "it's basically an invalid kind of value for class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 96.303,
          "en": "which is why we're getting this warning here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 101.07,
          "en": "That's why when adding a class name conditionally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.07,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "you should use this ternary expression approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 104.85300000000001,
          "en": "for doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.5,
          "end": 108.93,
          "en": "Now, of course, it's also possible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.93,
          "end": 113.13,
          "en": "that you maybe wanna add a class dynamically to an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 116.973,
          "en": "that also already has a class that should always be applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.02000000000001,
          "end": 120.84,
          "en": "Let's say here on this email label,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 122.65,
          "en": "there we could add className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.51,
          "end": 125.16,
          "en": "and let's say this label here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.16,
          "end": 127.353,
          "en": "should always have a label class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.28,
          "end": 130.53,
          "en": "It's not really needed in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.53,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "but, of course, it could absolutely be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 135.153,
          "en": "that such a label class is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.11,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "And this class should always be applied",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.913,
          "en": "not just when a certain condition is met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "But let's now say that in addition to this label class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 149.34,
          "en": "we wanna add the invalid class to this label here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.34,
          "end": 153.273,
          "en": "if an invalid value was entered into this input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 157.5,
          "en": "Because indeed in the CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.5,
          "end": 160.8,
          "en": "I provided to you in the index.css file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.8,
          "end": 165.12,
          "en": "I got a rule that does change the color of the label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.12,
          "end": 167.19299999999998,
          "en": "if it has an invalid clause.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.3,
          "end": 170.01,
          "en": "And we could also change this rule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.01,
          "end": 171.99,
          "en": "to look for a label clause",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.99,
          "end": 175.14,
          "en": "that then also has the invalid clause in addition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.14,
          "end": 178.623,
          "en": "so that we do indeed need this label class as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 181.44,
          "en": "Now with that, if I save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.44,
          "end": 183.96,
          "en": "you see that now this label is red,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.96,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "but, of course, now it's always red",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 188.463,
          "en": "because I'm always adding the invalid class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.84,
          "en": "So to add this class conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.84,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "and merge it with this class which is always required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 201.07,
          "en": "you can simply set the value here on className dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 202.2,
          "end": 207.2,
          "en": "and set it to a template literal by using back ticks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.07999999999998,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "So not single quotes, but this special back tick character",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 213.423,
          "en": "you find on your keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.5,
          "end": 217.89,
          "en": "This is another way of creating strings in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.89,
          "end": 221.67000000000002,
          "en": "And when using this approach for creating strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.67000000000002,
          "end": 225.21,
          "en": "you can use a special JavaScript syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.21,
          "end": 226.35,
          "en": "this dollar sign",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.35,
          "end": 229.89,
          "en": "followed by opening and closing curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.89,
          "end": 233.103,
          "en": "to inject dynamic values into that string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.838,
          "end": 237.51,
          "en": "And this allows you to construct a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.51,
          "end": 241.6,
          "en": "that includes both hard-coded values like this label here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.67,
          "end": 246.21,
          "en": "as well as dynamically injected values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 246.21,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "And you can inject as many values as you need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 251.523,
          "en": "to construct a longer string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 256.21,
          "en": "And therefore here, we could then check if emailNotValid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.4,
          "end": 260.94,
          "en": "and if that's the case, inject the invalid class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.94,
          "end": 265.94,
          "en": "and otherwise an empty string into this string here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.34,
          "end": 269.4,
          "en": "so that this overall string is always a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.4,
          "end": 271,
          "en": "that includes the word label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 271.86,
          "end": 276.18,
          "en": "and then separated by a white space either the word invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.18,
          "end": 281.18,
          "en": "if this condition here is met or nothing else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.69,
          "end": 283.65,
          "en": "And therefore, with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 286.02,
          "en": "you'll see that if I saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.02,
          "end": 290.76,
          "en": "by default, the label has this grayish look here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.76,
          "end": 294.63,
          "en": "But if I click Sign In without entering a valid value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 294.63,
          "end": 297.73,
          "en": "you see that it does get this invalid style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 299.49,
          "end": 303.3,
          "en": "and that's therefore how you can merge such styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 303.3,
          "end": 306.51,
          "en": "and how you can add some classes conditionally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 306.51,
          "end": 308.523,
          "en": "and other classes permanently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 309.93,
          "end": 313.38,
          "en": "And, of course, we can therefore also copy and paste this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 313.38,
          "end": 317.163,
          "en": "down here to the password label and add it there as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.57,
          "end": 320.68,
          "en": "so that now if you save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.66,
          "end": 323.64,
          "en": "and you reload and click Sign In",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 323.64,
          "end": 327.69,
          "en": "without entering valid values in either of these two fields,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 327.69,
          "end": 331.323,
          "en": "both labels are now highlighted, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 332.49,
          "end": 335.07,
          "en": "and that's how you can apply styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 335.07,
          "end": 339.483,
          "en": "dynamically conditionally with vanilla CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}